{"id":"n-20261009-s6oiv8","category":"sports","display_title":"Maccabi Israel Honors Top Athletes","display_title_he":"מכבי ישראל הוקירה ספורטאים מצטיינים","short_summary":"Maccabi Israel celebrated its standout athletes and teams in a grand gala event in Ra'anana, featuring special tributes and a review of upcoming developmental projects.","english_level":"C1","words":604,"reading_time":4,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Ynet","domain":"ynet.co.il","url":"https://www.ynet.co.il/sport/article/byq87ahjml","title":"ערב של כוכבים: מכבי ישראל הצדיעה לספורטאים המצטיינים","published_at":"2026-10-09T03:30:00.000Z"},{"name":"Walla","domain":"sports.walla.co.il","url":"https://sports.walla.co.il/item/3871492","title":"ערב של כוכבים: מכבי ישראל הצדיעה למצטייני השנה","published_at":"2026-10-09T07:46:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-09T03:30:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:24:05.018Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Maccabi Israel recently hosted a vibrant and emotionally charged tribute gala at the Ra'anana Amphitheater, drawing more than one thousand athletes, coaching staff, management teams, and prominent figures from across the Israeli sports landscape. The evening was dedicated to celebrating remarkable local and international achievements accomplished by Maccabi athletes and clubs over the past year.","A central emotional highlight of the ceremony was a heartfelt tribute paid to Israeli basketball icon Mickey Berkowitz. Attended by his sons, Roy and Niv, and his grandchildren, the homage underscored Berkowitz's legendary status, his famous winning fast break, and his enduring impact on Maccabi Tel Aviv and the national team. Naor Galili, the CEO of Maccabi Israel, praised Berkowitz as a true winner on and off the court who consistently embodied the core values of the organization, while the assembly offered prayers for his health.","During his address, Galili also surveyed several strategic initiatives and milestones for 2026. Among them was the visionary \"Maccabi of Israel 2032\" project, designed to scout and develop the next generation of athletic talent under a committee led by former Olympic stars Alex Shtilov, Nicol Zelikman, and Eitan Urbach. Additional presentations highlighted the \"Maccabi Market\" retail platform, technological innovations developed through partnerships with Vertex to provide advanced professional tools, corporate governance reforms within sports federations pursued alongside the Ministry of Culture and Sport, and a pioneering digital protection initiative for athletes carried out alongside Look On Cam.","The event opened with remarks from Yigal Carmi, Chairman of Maccabi Israel, and Culture and Sport Minister Miki Zohar. Reflecting on his tenure, Minister Zohar spoke about four years of genuine partnership with the sporting community, unprecedented budgetary allocations that advanced Israeli sports, and his respect for democratic processes as his current term concludes, expressing how much he would miss the community.","Hosted by Liron Cohen and Or Shiniuk, the gala featured video messages from basketball star Roman Sorkin alongside greetings from swimmers and players like Anastasia Gorbenko, Deni Avdija, and Manor Solomon. The evening culminated in a high-energy musical performance led by Dalit Rechester, Anna Zak, and Subliminal, while special tokens of appreciation were distributed to various business partners and production teams.","A vast array of individual athletes and clubs received recognition for stellar competitive performances. Olympic gymnast Artem Dolgopyat received special acclaim alongside his personal coach, Sergei Weissburg. Other honorees included rhythmic gymnast Daniela Munitz, who earned a bronze medal at the senior European championships, alongside group team members Arina Gvodzky, Sofia Prezhin, and Taisia Sokolenko, supported by coaches Ella Samopulov, Natasha Osmulov, and Moran Buzovsky. Further recognition celebrated achievements in fencing, European and world titles in acrobatics by Haifa Flyers and Maccabi Acrogym, and eleven medals won by world champions in obstacle course racing led by Gil Marantz, Adam Malki, and Itay Wolf. Judoka Yitzhak Ashpiz was honored for capturing gold at the senior European championships and the Budapest Grand Slam, alongside youth European bronze medalist Ya-Lee Zarkovsky. Marathon runner Gashau Ayale, who secured a European bronze and team gold alongside Maru Teferi and Tadu Abuhay, was celebrated alongside archer Itai Shani, an Olympic bronze medalist at the world championships.","Numerous championship-winning teams were likewise honored across multiple sports categories. These included Israeli swimming champions Maccabi Haifa Carmel for both men and women, Maccabi Tel Aviv rugby teams, women's volleyball double champions Maccabi Ashdod, Ramat Hasharon Hammerheads in football, and Sharon handball double champions A.S. Ramat Hasharon for men and Bnot Herzelia for women. Additional club honorees featured State Cup holders Maccabi Ironi Ramat Gan in women's basketball and Maccabi Tel Aviv in football, represented by striker Elad Madmon and legal advisor Moran Meiri."],"facts":[{"fact":"Maccabi Israel held a large tribute gala at the Ra'anana Amphitheater with over 1,000 athletes, management teams, and sports executives.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The event honored domestic and international achievements, alongside a special tribute to basketball legend Mickey Berkowitz.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Maccabi Israel CEO Naor Galili outlined initiatives including the 'Maccabi of Israel 2032' project led by former Olympic athletes Alex Shtilov, Nicol Zelikman, and Eitan Urbach.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Culture and Sport Minister Miki Zohar attended and reflected on his four-year tenure and record sports funding.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Numerous athletes and teams across gymnastics, fencing, acrobatics, ninja obstacle courses, judo, marathon running, archery, and team sports received recognition.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Maccabi","lemma":"Maccabi","pos":"PROPN","he":"מכבי","name":"true"},{"text":"Israel","lemma":"Israel","pos":"PROPN","he":"ישראל","name":"true"},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"ADV","he":"לאחרונה","name":false},{"text":"hosted","lemma":"host","pos":"VERB","he":"אירח","name":false},{"text":"vibrant","lemma":"vibrant","pos":"ADJ","he":"תוסס","name":false},{"text":"and","lemma":"and","pos":"CCONJ","he":"ו־","name":false},{"text":"emotionally","lemma":"emotionally","pos":"ADV","he":"רגשית","name":false},{"text":"charged","lemma":"charge","pos":"ADJ","he":"טעון","name":false},{"text":"tribute","lemma":"tribute","pos":"NOUN","he":"הוקרה","name":false},{"text":"gala","lemma":"gala","pos":"NOUN","he":"אירוע חגיגי","name":false},{"text":"at","lemma":"at","pos":"ADP","he":"ב־","name":false},{"text":"the","lemma":"the","pos":"DET","he":"ה־","name":false},{"text":"Ra'anana","lemma":"Ra'anana","pos":"PROPN","he":"רעננה","name":"true"},{"text":"Amphitheater","lemma":"amphitheater","pos":"NOUN","he":"אמפי פארק","name":"true"},{"text":"drawing","lemma":"draw","pos":"VERB","he":"שמושך / משך","name":false},{"text":"more","lemma":"more","pos":"ADV","he":"יותר","name":false},{"text":"than","lemma":"than","pos":"ADP","he":"מ־","name":false},{"text":"one","lemma":"one","pos":"NUM","he":"אחד","name":false},{"text":"thousand","lemma":"thousand","pos":"NUM","he":"אלף","name":false},{"text":"athletes","lemma":"athlete","pos":"NOUN","he":"ספורטאים","name":false},{"text":"coaching","lemma":"coaching","pos":"NOUN","he":"אימון","name":false},{"text":"staff","lemma":"staff","pos":"NOUN","he":"סגל","name":false},{"text":"management","lemma":"management","pos":"NOUN","he":"ניהול","name":false},{"text":"teams","lemma":"team","pos":"NOUN","he":"קבוצות","name":false},{"text":"prominent","lemma":"prominent","pos":"ADJ","he":"בכירים","name":false},{"text":"figure